(LST2-06 — "each element renders exactly as it does when printed
 individually: text elements are quoted". The two halves of that sentence
 disagree: a text prints bare on its own and quoted inside a list. See
 Discrepancy 8.
 Also covers: LST2-08 (floats and numbers render as usual, 2.0 keeping its
 trailing .0 in both positions), LST2-07 (a boolean renders 1 in both).
 Ran: VOX_CORE_PATH=/home/josj/scr/english/vox/coreasm /home/josj/scr/english/vox/target/release/vox LST2-06.vox -o p && ./p
 expected output:
   alpha
   2.0
   1
   ["alpha", 2.0, 1]
   ["1"]
   [1]
)
a text called word is "alpha".
a decimal called round is 2.0.
a boolean called ok is yes.
print word.
print round.
print ok.
a list called packed is [word, round, ok].
print packed.
a list called quoted is ["1"].
a list called bare is [1].
print quoted.
print bare.
